Package: labeloxav
Version: @VERSION@
Section: science
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: docker.io | docker-ce, docker-compose-v2 | docker-compose-plugin, curl
Recommends: openssl
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Maintainer: Sherin Joseph Roy <sherin.srambickal@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://sherin-sef-ai.github.io/LabeloxAV/
Description: India-native data engine for autonomous driving
 LabeloxAV turns dashcam and sensor footage into labelled training data:
 auto-labelling behind a confidence gate, human review, object tracking,
 3D from LiDAR or estimated depth, HD map export, and a governed
 retraining loop. The ontology is built for Indian roads.
 .
 This package installs the source tree under /opt/labeloxav and the
 `labeloxav` command. The product itself runs as Docker containers built
 from that tree; run `sudo labeloxav install` once, then open
 http://localhost:3000. No GPU is required for annotation, review, search
 and export. Model paths that need CUDA refuse rather than pretend.
